 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the union of shortest paths from each ",
 StyleBox["ui", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["vi", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"cfb75cb8-e9c7-41c5-a664-d5f727750599"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The spray at ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " has an edge ",
 StyleBox["u \[RightArrow] v", "TI"],
 " for every edge ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v) = d(c, u) + 1", "TI"],
 ". Edges inside one shell about ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " are dropped."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"43147844-a67f-4e89-b045-e723e7ee44f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The directed paths from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " are exactly the shortest paths from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 ". The paths from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " to a sink are the maximal ones: a sink is a vertex with no neighbour \
farther from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 ". The spray is the graph analogue of the exponential map at ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fb6dce7c-31d6-4d58-8f98-29d9d66e5f24"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On a bipartite graph such as the square grid no edge lies inside a shell, \
so the spray keeps every edge of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"47f0e46f-c5ac-436c-9f60-af859b8005b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With several sources ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v)", "TI"],
 " is replaced by ",
 StyleBox["d(C, v) = min d(c\:1d62, v)", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7db3bc46-dfb7-412f-872c-f4e5a5fb9db4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pair form picks shortest paths from each ",
 StyleBox["u\:1d62", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["v\:1d62", "TI"],
 " and takes the union of their path graphs."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a312f24c-a46b-4e65-ba5d-f9921e8c8860"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The spray keeps the vertex coordinates of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bc939d86-1fd4-49da-b76d-a647e5fbcd11"],

